# KNOWN GAP — Core #8 + Core #10: `gg check` ACCEPTS this, then BOTH Rust
# backends ICE. The self-host compiles and runs it CORRECTLY (a succession
# milestone: the reference lags the self-host).
#
#   gg check              : exit 0, "OK: no semantic errors"
#   gg build (C)          : exit 101 -- internal compiler panic
#   gg build --backend=llvm: exit 101 -- identical
#   self-host             : compiles, prints `ab`, exit 0
#
# The panic:
#   [move-follow-through] 1 violation(s):
#     @main::bb0::i1 -- Move-mode assign _2 = move _1: source is
#     drop-registered but is not MoveZero'd before the next drop site
#   panicked at src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:1872
#
# INTENDED: `ab`, exit 0.
#
# THE TRIGGER IS **DROPPABLE INNER x COMPUTED INITIALIZER**. Both axes measured
# 2026-08-05, and neither `async` nor `spawn` nor `&` is required -- the repro
# above is a plain `void main()`, minimized from an earlier over-specified
# `async` form:
#     shared String s = "a" + "b"    <-- ICE 101  (droppable + computed)
#     shared String s = "hello"      <-- exit 0   (rodata literal, cap=0)
#     shared int    n = 1 + 2        <-- exit 0   (scalar inner, computed)
# Every `shared` fixture in the corpus uses the literal form. Core #12
# axis-incompleteness on the INITIALIZER axis: one value sampled, and it is
# the one that happens to work.
#
# SCOPE: one cell. Sibling shapes measured the same day, same panic site:
#   - with `spawn bump(&s)` + `t.await()`: ICE 101 on both backends, and the
#     SELF-HOST double-frees (see shared_spawn_amp_param_double_free.gg) --
#     so that shape is broken on BOTH lanes, in different ways.
#   - `shared Vector[int]` + spawn + read: same ICE.
#
# Graduate out of known_gaps/ (un-ignore + move) the round this is fixed.

void main():
    shared String s = "a" + "b"
    print(s)
